   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE_13">via Sanità, 2, III </name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE">Trieste</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Σάς εὔχαριστώ πολὺ δία τὴν εὔγενίαν σάς. Πολλὰ <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">χρόνια</seg>!</p> <closer>
                        <salute>ὄ φίλος σάς</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <date when="1919-12-31">31.xii.919</date>
                    </closer>
                </div>
                <div type="translation">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE_13">Via Sanità, 2, III </name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE">Trieste</name> </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>  <p>Thank you very much for your kindness. <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">Many years!</seg>
                    </p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Your friend,</salute>
                        <signed>James Joyce</signed>
                        <date when="1919-12-31">31.xii.919</date>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">The postcard image is of “VENEZIA – Notte in Laguna” (“Venice – Night in the Lagoon”). The painter is Gian Luciano Sormani (1867-1938), born in Legnano, Italy, and a student of Pompeo Molmenti (1819-1894). Sormani was a painter and bookbinder who settled in Venice and was known for pencil-and-watercolor scenes of Venetian lagoon daily life. His work appeared on numerous postcards produced by Stabilimento Litografico A. Scrocchi, a lithography publishing company founded by Attilio Scrocchi around 1880 in Milan.</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ’s idiosyncratic spelling is retained for the texts he writes in Greek.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">“Many years” is a common phrase for greetings in Greek and translates approximately as “wishing you a long life”. Thanks to Stephanie Nelson for assistance with the Greek.</note> </div>
